# MF Overhaul 0.4.3: user screenshot: tall beaded columns of grey spheres rising far above the trees. Those are the burning-vehicle
#   and fire smoke rows (smoke, smoke_burn, smoke_filler, smoke_mid, smoke_fuel ...), which 0.4.0 made buoyant (+0.05 .. +0.3). Over
#   a 60-130 s life that lifts each puff hundreds of metres and strings the continuous emission into separate balls. The column
#   shape of a real fire plume comes from steady emission and wind, so: vertical accel back to the vanilla values (smoke +0.1,
#   smoke_sm +0.05, choke +0.1, smoke_burn +0.01, smoke_filler -0.01, smoke_mid +0.03, smoke_fuel +0.07, fuel_smoke -0.5,
#   smoke_fbomb -0.02, smoke_flam -0.05), emission doubled so the plume is continuous (smoke_burn 1 -> 2, smoke 3 -> 5, smoke_big
#   5 -> 8, smoke_mid 3 -> 5), spin 60 -> 30. Sooty palette from 0.4.0 kept.
